---
import Mark from '../../components/mark/logos/c07.astro';
import {
  CATEGORIES,
  COVERAGE_STATES,
  DESTINATIONS,
  DURABILITY,
  FAQ,
  FORMATS,
  GITHUB_URL,
  MCP_TOOLS,
  NOT_YET,
  PROMISES,
  SITE,
  STEPS,
  WORKING,
} from '../../data/site';

const categoryHues = Object.fromEntries(CATEGORIES.map(({ key, hue }) => [key, hue]));
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
      name: 'Hozz',
      applicationCategory: 'HealthApplication',
      operatingSystem: 'iOS, macOS',
      url: SITE,
      downloadUrl: GITHUB_URL,
      isAccessibleForFree: true,
      license: `${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`,
      description:
        'A free, open-source iPhone app with a companion Mac app that exports Apple Health data to destinations you own.',
      softwareHelp: `${SITE}/#faq`,
    },
    {
      '@type': 'FAQPage',
      mainEntity: FAQ.map(({ q, a }) => ({
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: q,
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
      })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Hozz makes a durable copy of your Apple Health history in files and systems you control."
    />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#eef0c8" />
    <title>Hozz — A copy costs the original nothing</title>
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Hozz, back to top">
        <Mark size={28} />
        <span>Hozz</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#export">How to export</a>
        <a href="#destinations">Destinations</a>
        <a href="#honest">Trust</a>
        <a class="source-link" href={GITHUB_URL}>View source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="kicker">A field guide to keeping your health history</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">A copy costs the <em>original</em> nothing.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Hozz makes your Apple Health history exist somewhere you also control. Your
            original stays exactly where it is.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button" href="#export">See how it copies</a>
            <span>Free · open source · early alpha</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="copy-study">
          <div class="rings" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="ring ring-4">
              <span class="ring-label label-mac">Mac</span>
              <span class="ring-label label-folder">folder</span>
              <div class="ring ring-3">
                <span class="ring-label label-ha">Home Assistant</span>
                <span class="ring-label label-mqtt">MQTT</span>
                <div class="ring ring-2">
                  <span class="ring-label label-web">web</span>
                  <span class="ring-label label-influx">InfluxDB</span>
                  <div class="ring ring-1">
                    <div class="core">
                      <Mark size={62} />
                      <span>Apple Health<br />stays whole</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            One kept source. As many useful copies as you choose.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="principle">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">The useful distinction</p>
          <h2>Not extraction. <em>Multiplication.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Export usually sounds like removal. Hozz only reads Apple Health. It never writes
          back, changes a record or chooses a destination for you. Nothing leaves your phone
          until you add one and confirm it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter" id="export" aria-labelledby="export-title">
        <div class="chapter-heading">
          <p class="section-label">How do I export my Apple Health data?</p>
          <h2 id="export-title">Plant the copy once.</h2>
          <p>
            Install Hozz on your iPhone, then make three choices. After that, new records
            copy automatically when iOS gives Hozz time to run.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps">
          {STEPS.map((step, index) => (
            <li style={`--step-hue: ${categoryHues[step.category]}`}>
              <span class="step-number">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <div>
                <h3>{step.title}</h3>
                <p>{step.body}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <aside class="answer-note">
          <strong>Before you begin</strong>
          <p>
            Hozz is early alpha. It works, but Health type coverage is still partial. Apple
            decides when background work runs, and Health cannot be read while your phone is
            locked.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter tinted" id="destinations" aria-labelledby="destinations-title">
        <div class="chapter-heading">
          <p class="section-label">Where the copies live</p>
          <h2 id="destinations-title">Six places. <em>All yours.</em></h2>
          <p>
            There is no Hozz cloud in the middle. Choose one destination or several; each
            keeps its own place in the queue.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="destination-grid">
          {DESTINATIONS.map((destination) => (
            <li>
              <span
                class="destination-dot"
                style={`--item-hue: ${categoryHues[destination.category]}`}
                aria-hidden="true"
              />
              <h3>{destination.title}</h3>
              <p>{destination.body}</p>
              <code>{destination.fact}</code>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter formats" aria-labelledby="formats-title">
        <div class="chapter-heading">
          <p class="section-label">What comes out</p>
          <h2 id="formats-title">A file you can keep.</h2>
          <p>
            Seven shapes for the same purpose: data that remains useful without Hozz.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Format</th>
                <th scope="col">Made for</th>
                <th scope="col">Fidelity</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {FORMATS.map((format) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">{format.name}</th>
                  <td data-label="Made for">{format.use}</td>
                  <td data-label="Fidelity">
                    <span class:list={{ warning: format.note.startsWith('Lossy') }}>
                      {format.note}
                    </span>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter durability" id="honest" aria-labelledby="durability-title">
        <div class="chapter-heading light-heading">
          <p class="section-label">Why the copy holds</p>
          <h2 id="durability-title">Interruption can repeat work. It cannot skip records.</h2>
          <p>
            Hozz moves an anchor only after records are durably staged. That quiet rule is
            the foundation of every export.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="durability-grid">
          {DURABILITY.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <code>{item.fact}</code>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p>{item.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <div class="test-strip">
          <strong>475</strong>
          <span>XCTest tests exercise the details behind that promise.</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter honesty" aria-labelledby="honesty-title">
        <div class="chapter-heading">
          <p class="section-label">Honest coverage</p>
          <h2 id="honesty-title">No green tick for an unknown.</h2>
          <p>
            Apple will not let an app distinguish “you denied this type” from “you have no
            data.” Hozz names the ambiguity instead of guessing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <dl class="states">
          {COVERAGE_STATES.map((item) => (
            <div class={`state state-${item.tone}`}>
              <dt>{item.state}</dt>
              <dd>{item.body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>
        <ul class="promises" aria-label="Privacy promises">
          {PROMISES.map((promise) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{promise.title}</strong>
              <span>{promise.body}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter assistant" aria-labelledby="assistant-title">
        <div class="assistant-copy">
          <p class="section-label">A local field assistant</p>
          <h2 id="assistant-title">Ask your copy. <em>Read only.</em></h2>
          <p>
            The companion Mac app includes an MCP server. Your own assistant can query the
            local database, but the server cannot change or delete anything.
          </p>
          <aside>
            <strong>The important caveat</strong>
            <p>
              A cloud assistant may upload whatever it reads. That is the assistant’s
              behaviour, not Hozz’s.
            </p>
          </aside>
        </div>
        <div class="specimen" aria-label="Things the MCP server can query">
          <div class="specimen-top">
            <span>local database</span>
            <span>permission: read</span>
          </div>
          <ul>
            {MCP_TOOLS.map((tool) => <li>{tool}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter status" id="status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
        <div class="chapter-heading">
          <p class="section-label">Field notes · early alpha</p>
          <h2 id="status-title">It works. It is not finished.</h2>
          <p>Both statements belong together. The repository is the record.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="status-columns">
          <div>
            <h3>Working now</h3>
            <ul>
              {WORKING.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Not yet</h3>
            <ul>
              {NOT_YET.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
        <div class="chapter-heading">
          <p class="section-label">Plain answers</p>
          <h2 id="faq-title">Before you make a copy.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          {FAQ.map((item) => (
            <details>
              <summary>{item.q}</summary>
              <p>{item.a}</p>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
        <Mark size={72} />
        <p class="section-label">Free forever · GPL-3.0</p>
        <h2 id="closing-title">Keep what your body recorded.</h2>
        <p>
          Hozz is being built in the open by Brandon Moore. Read every line before you trust
          it with a single record.
        </p>
        <a class="button button-light" href={GITHUB_URL}>Read the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <a class="brand" href="#top">
        <Mark size={28} />
        <span>Hozz</span>
      </a>
      <p>Your history, growing somewhere you control.</p>
      <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Erode';
    src: url('/fonts/erode-g-400.woff2') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Erode';
    src: url('/fonts/erode-g-500.woff2') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 500;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'General Sans';
    src: url('/fonts/general-sans-400.woff2') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'General Sans';
    src: url('/fonts/general-sans-600.woff2') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 600;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono';
    src: url('/fonts/ibm-plex-mono-400.woff2') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  :root {
    --ink: #33382b;
    --deep: #555f44;
    --sage: #818c68;
    --leaf: #b4bf8e;
    --glow: #eef0c8;
    --ground: #f5f3e8;
    --paper: #fbfaf3;
    --line: rgba(51, 56, 43, 0.23);
    --measure: 72rem;
    --gutter: clamp(1.15rem, 4vw, 4rem);
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
    background: var(--ground);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    font-family: 'General Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    background:
      linear-gradient(rgba(51, 56, 43, 0.026) 1px, transparent 1px),
      var(--ground);
    background-size: 100% 2rem;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.22em;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  :focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #33382b;
    outline-offset: 4px;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  h1,
  h2 {
    font-family: 'Erode', serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  h1 em,
  h2 em {
    color: var(--deep);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(3.6rem, 7.8vw, 7.9rem);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 5rem);
  }

  h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  code,
  .section-label,
  .step-number,
  .specimen {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
  }

  .site-header,
  footer {
    width: min(100%, calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter)));
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
  }

  .site-header {
    display: flex;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 10;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    min-height: 5.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .brand {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .brand svg {
    flex: none;
  }

  nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(1rem, 2.7vw, 2.3rem);
    font-size: 0.84rem;
  }

  nav a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .source-link {
    padding: 0.58rem 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .hero,
  .chapter,
  .principle,
  .closing {
    padding-inline: max(var(--gutter), calc((100vw - var(--measure)) / 2));
  }

  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.07fr) minmax(24rem, 0.93fr);
    align-items: center;
    min-height: min(53rem, calc(100vh - 5.5rem));
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 7rem);
  }

  .kicker,
  .section-label {
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--deep);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.2rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.55rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--deep);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 3.2rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--glow);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .button:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--leaf);
  }

  .copy-study {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .rings {
    display: grid;
    position: relative;
    place-items: center;
    width: min(100%, 34rem);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .ring {
    display: grid;
    position: relative;
    place-items: center;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border: 1px solid;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .ring-4 {
    width: 100%;
    border-color: var(--sage);
    background: rgba(180, 191, 142, 0.12);
  }

  .ring-3 {
    width: 76%;
    border-color: var(--sage);
    background: rgba(180, 191, 142, 0.15);
  }

  .ring-2 {
    width: 68%;
    border-color: var(--deep);
    background: rgba(238, 240, 200, 0.4);
  }

  .ring-1 {
    width: 60%;
    border-color: var(--deep);
    background: var(--glow);
  }

  .core {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: clamp(0.52rem, 1.25vw, 0.7rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .core svg {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .ring-label {
    position: absolute;
    padding: 0.18rem 0.42rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--sage);
    background: var(--paper);
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: clamp(0.5rem, 1vw, 0.65rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .label-mac {
    top: 8%;
    left: 19%;
  }

  .label-folder {
    right: 2%;
    bottom: 26%;
  }

  .label-ha {
    top: 43%;
    left: -12%;
  }

  .label-mqtt {
    top: 14%;
    right: 2%;
  }

  .label-web {
    right: -12%;
    bottom: 25%;
  }

  .label-influx {
    bottom: -5%;
    left: 12%;
  }

  .copy-study figcaption {
    max-width: 25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem auto 0;
    color: var(--deep);
    font-family: 'Erode', serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .principle {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 0.75fr);
    padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem);
    color: var(--glow);
    background: var(--deep);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 8rem);
  }

  .principle .section-label,
  .light-heading .section-label,
  .closing .section-label {
    color: var(--glow);
  }

  .principle h2 {
    max-width: 13ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .principle h2 em,
  .light-heading h2 em {
    color: var(--glow);
  }

  .principle > p {
    align-self: end;
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.7vw, 1.35rem);
  }

  .chapter {
    padding-block: clamp(5.5rem, 11vw, 10rem);
  }

  .chapter-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(18rem, 0.62fr);
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    column-gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 8rem);
  }

  .chapter-heading .section-label {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .chapter-heading h2 {
    max-width: 14ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .chapter-heading > p:last-child {
    align-self: end;
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--deep);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .steps li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 1.6rem clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 2rem) 2rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .steps li + li {
    padding-left: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .step-number {
    color: var(--deep);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
  }

  .steps h3 {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'Erode', serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .steps p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--deep);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .steps li::before {
    content: '';
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    width: 2.8rem;
    height: 0.35rem;
    background: var(--step-hue);
  }

  .answer-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 11rem 1fr;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 1.35rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--sage);
    background: rgba(238, 240, 200, 0.4);
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .answer-note p {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tinted {
    background: var(--glow);
  }

  .destination-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--deep);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .destination-grid li {
    display: flex;
    min-width: 0;
    min-height: 17rem;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--deep);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--deep);
  }

  .destination-grid li:nth-child(3n) {
    border-right: 0;
  }

  .destination-dot {
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--item-hue);
  }

  .destination-grid h3 {
    font-family: 'Erode', serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .destination-grid p {
    color: var(--deep);
